 ## Overview
-MAtCha is a method for high-quality avatar generation from sparse views, specifically designed to handle scenarios with minimal view overlap [S1][S2, unofficial]. It employs an atlas-of-charts and depth estimation as input to an MLP, which deforms the atlas and produces high-quality meshes represented with 2D Gaussians [S1][S2, unofficial]. It is distinguished from sibling methods like CoR-GS by its reliance on an atlas-based deformation pipeline rather than independent reconstruction comparisons, and from FFN-based approaches by its use of an MLP for geometric deformation [S1][S2, unofficial].
